  "title": "Make budget parsing linear on untrusted request text",
  "file": "src/pipeline/budget.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A request contains many repeated, unfinished details tags. When delivery parses it, the factory's shared event loop stalls, preventing other runs and server requests from progressing; larger inputs make the interruption quadratically longer.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun -e 'import { statedBudget } from \"./src/pipeline/budget.ts\"; for (const kib of [128,256,512,1024]) { const prompt = \"<details \".repeat(Math.ceil(kib*1024/9)).slice(0,kib*1024); const begin = performance.now(); const result = statedBudget(prompt); console.log(JSON.stringify({bytes:prompt.length,elapsed_ms:Math.round(performance.now()-begin),result})); }'",
    "output": "Equivalent code executed in a throwaway script under $TMPDIR:\n{\"bytes\":131072,\"elapsed_ms\":225,\"result\":null}\n{\"bytes\":262144,\"elapsed_ms\":895,\"result\":null}\n{\"bytes\":524288,\"elapsed_ms\":3585,\"result\":null}\n{\"bytes\":1048576,\"elapsed_ms\":14295,\"result\":null}"
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD line 30 uses `.split(/(<\\/?details\\b[^>]*>)/gi)`. Each unfinished prefix causes another scan of the remaining suffix looking for `>`. The timings show approximately quadrupled runtime for doubled input. Delivery calls `statedBudget(ctx.run.prompt, redact)` synchronously at engine.ts:2752, so its surrounding try/catch cannot interrupt this work. The parser and delivery call are absent at base."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Someone files an issue whose body repeats an unclosed `<details ` opening thousands of times. Delivery then stalls synchronously while it parses the budget, and the time grows with the square of the text length. GitHub caps issue and comment bodies at 65,536 characters, so the real worst case is about 56 ms per render; only a very large hand-started prompt, which the operator writes and trusts, reaches seconds.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/adj/r.ts and bun $TMPDIR/adj/r2.ts (both call statedBudget on the string '<details ' repeated)",
    "output": "128 KB 224 ms null\n256 KB 894 ms null\n512 KB 3564 ms null\n65529 chars 56 ms"
   },
   "evidence": "budget.ts:30 `.split(/(<\\/?details\\b[^>]*>)/gi)`: when a `<details` prefix has no closing `>`, `[^>]*` scans to the end of the input, and the scan repeats for each later prefix, so the work is quadratic. The code is new in this change; base has no budget.ts. Its only caller is engine.ts:2752 `statedBudget(ctx.run.prompt, redact)`, once per delivery render."
  }
 },
